    "notes": {
        "f3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001": {
            "x": 144,
            "y": -288,
            "width": 640,
            "height": 352,
            "content": "## Project status → pipeline\n\nThe dispatcher of the status-driven connector pipeline (Appmixer-ai/appmixer-components#2890, step 1 in #2916).\n\n`On Project Item Changed` receives `projects_v2_item` deliveries (action `edited`) through the GitHub connector's endpoint `/plugins/appmixer/github/events`, at which an organization owner points one organization webhook (github connector README). The bound account needs only `read:org` and `read:project`. `Status changed` keeps only moves of the Status field.\n\n`Resolve the item` is one GraphQL call on the card's content node; `Pipeline event` turns it into `{issue?, pr?, connector, branch, status, from, runId}` — an issue is linked to its PR through the closing keyword, a PR card looks up no issue, the connector comes from the `appmixer:<x>` label. `runId` is deterministic (card, target status, `updated_at`), so a redelivery is recognised.\n\n**Source of truth:** `.github/appmixer-flows/project-status-pipeline.json` in the connectors repo."
        },
        "f3000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002": {
            "x": 1104,
            "y": 288,
            "width": 640,
            "height": 240,
            "content": "### One comment per item\n\n`Comments on the item` reads the item's comments, `Pipeline comment` finds the one with `<!-- pipeline: {...} -->`, ends on a run id already recorded (`duplicate`), otherwise rewrites the comment with the new move. `Write the pipeline comment` creates or edits it (POST / PATCH). The comment goes to the issue when the card is an issue, else to the PR.\n\nThis version starts nothing else. The stage branches (Testing, Review, Doc&Verification, Needs input) hang on `Pipeline event` → `Resolved`."
        }
    },
